ot restate them and the general text says no record of the Techs exists. No starting_money stored; the book prints no sum for the Tech. || HEADING: Monkey Boy Tech R.C.C. under Monkey Boys, an engineered mutant animal and a race. sdc_base is stated (a formula on P.E., printed without ''plus those gained from skills''), so there is no men_of_arms line. || XP: the ladder headed Monkey Boy Tech, Simvan Monster Rider on the unnumbered Experience Tables page after printed 174 (cache p176). || NATURAL SKILLS: Climbing 75 and Gymnastics 60 at per_level 0, as on the Soldier (judgement: printed as flat natural abilities). || SKILLS: Speaks and is literate in American at 98%: Language: Native Tongue 98 and Literacy: Native Language 98, per_level 0. Language: speaks one of choice (+20%) as a choice of one from the catalog''s Rifts tongues plus Language: Other, bonus 20. Basic Math 45+30 = 75. Advanced Math 45+20 = 65. Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Biology 30+20 = 50. Chemistry 30+20 = 50. Two Electrical skills of choice, one W.P. of choice. ''Three Medical or four Mechanical skills of choice'' is an either/or; stored as two variants, Medical training (three Medical picks) and Mechanical training (four Mechanical picks), each adding its choice group to the common list. Hand to Hand: Basic, no others available: hand_to_hand costs is empty. || RELATED: five, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Communications +10 with Cryptography printed at +15; Espionage is Forgery (+10%) and Intelligence (+5%) only, stored at the category''s +5; Rogue any except Streetwise with +10% to Computer Hacking only and no category bonus; Technical +10 with language skills printed at +15. The three differences are stated in the note for the player to add by hand. Physical ''except boxing, acrobatics and hand to hand'' stored as an except list naming those rows. Pilot, Pilot Related and Wilderness: none. Secondary: five at level one, plus two at levels 2, 4, 8, 10, 12 and 14, same list without bonuses. The runaway and free born allowance is a restriction line. || OPTIONAL DOG BOY TABLES: neither the general Monkey Boys text, the Soldier entry nor this entry mentions the Optional Dog Boy tables, so no restriction line is written for them."
